p. Those will be addressed.\r\n\r\nNoticed two other issues present in 4.1.\r\n\r\n1. If the payload is larger than 65495 for TCP, the length field in the IP packet is incorrect due to the length being a ushort. UDP will have a similar problem.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/155cec08-767f-4efc-a2c5-c9c04718bd75)\r\n2. When the PcapWriteHandler is attached to a TCP server, the FIN messages have incorrect segment and ack numbers. \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/236c3109-558d-4fa2-8cce-5fa05503ebc0)\r\n\r\n\r\nI will try to find the time to address these here with unit tests","For TCP, the payload can just be split into multiple PCAP entries. \r\nFor UDP, I imagine it could just log that it received too large of a payload.","Alright, all of the above have been handled. Tested large PCAP files and those show correctly in Wireshark now."],"path":"handler/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/pcap/TCPPacket.java","id":50497,"created_at":"2024-11-19T19:43:21Z","original_position":12,"side":"RIGHT","position":12,"submitted_on_commit":"da56043b982cfbcd160a40596859b9954ce3c478","diff_hunk":"@@ -36,13 +36,13 @@ private TCPPacket() {\n      * @param srcPort Source Port\n      * @param dstPort Destination Port\n      */\n-    static void writePacket(ByteBuf byteBuf, ByteBuf payload, int segmentNumber, int ackNumber, int srcPort,\n+    static void writePacket(ByteBuf byteBuf, ByteBuf payload, long segmentNumber, long ackNumber, int srcPort,\n                             int dstPort, TCPFlag... tcpFlags) {\n \n         byteBuf.writeShort(srcPort);     // Source Port\n         byteBuf.writeShort(dstPort);     // Destination Port\n-        byteBuf.writeInt(segmentNumber); // Segment Number\n-        byteBuf.writeInt(ackNumber);     // Acknowledgment Number\n+        byteBuf.writeInt((int) segmentNumber); // Segment Number","submitted_line":44},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change from `int` to `long` for `sendSegmentNumber` and `r